    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson** (77.16) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.32), our two most formidable starts against right-handed pitching. **Gunnar Henderson** faces Yesavage with a high-efficiency floor driven by a strong platoon advantage and a premium #2 spot in the order, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable 4.75 xERA matchup against Young and an elite xwOBA profile that overcomes the minor park drag. We are also capitalizing on the Merril Kelly start; the matchup against Arizona provides a significant boost for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.02) and **Curtis Mead** (62.15). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, in particular, thrives here due to a massive +14% platoon edge, while **Nasim Nunez** (60.80) remains a critical tactical start\u2014despite his #9 spot, his efficiency is propped up by a rare 87% stolen base success rate against Kelly\u2019s slow delivery, making him a high-leverage play in our scarcity-focused build.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Coby Mayo** (45.56), who narrowly missed the cut behind the more efficient profiles of **Brayan Rocchio** and **Liam Hicks**. While **Coby Mayo** projects well, his platoon disadvantage today capped his upside relative to the rest of the infield. Similarly, **Miguel Vargas** (43.76) was relegated to the bench; despite his raw talent, the combination of facing a high-skill arm in Luzardo and his specific platoon profile lowered his projection below the 40-point efficiency threshold for certain slots, and **Sam Antonacci** (36.66) fell entirely below our 40-point floor. Owners should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Nasim Nunez**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Curtis Mead**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**; while the optimizer has factored in historical landing spots, any unexpected shifts to the bottom of the order could dampen the projected output for these key contributors.",
